you know this is a story that we we  talked about on the radio side  and on the surface when i see the report  from zach rosenblatt of nj.com citing an  unnamed source that it's unlikely nick  foles will return to the eagles as a  backup my first reaction was to be a  little snarky be a little mean spirited  and say well of course it's unlikely  zach you're not telling us anything we  don't know  if likely is more than 50 and unlikely  is is less than 50 yes it's unlikely  that nick foles will be the backup to  carson wentz in 2019  especially if the eagles apply the  franchise tag to nick foles at what will  roughly be 25 million dollars for a  one-year salary when you've got carson  wentz in the fourth year of his rookie  contract and his base salary this year  is south of 1 million  it will be  problematic to say the least if you have  nick foles as his backup at 25 million  sends kind of a weird message to the  locker room if that's what you end up  doing  but  the more i looked at rosenblatt's story  there's there's enough meat there that  maybe we can begin the process of  connecting dots  and predicting the falling of dominoes  and maybe can glean  something significant because  in addition to  the comment that it's unlikely foles  will be the backup to carson wentz  rosenblatt points out that foles  probably would be interested in playing  for the giants probably i put that in  quotes because it was in quotes in his  story probably interested in the giants  that tells me this is coming from falls  or someone close to foals and this idea  of rattling the sword  about the giants  it it makes me think you know because a  week ago i said hey if the eagles are  going to apply the franchise tag to nick  foles for the sole purpose of trading  him they're violating the cba because  you're not allowed to  tag a guy simply to trade him you have  to have a good faith intention to employ  him at the amount of the tag which means  if you're going to tag nick foles as the  philadelphia eagles you have to intend  to pay him 25 million dollars to be the  backup to carson wentz but you know what  i poked around a little bit about that i  didn't get the impression that the the  falls camp was all that upset about the  prospect of being tagged and now i see  this  claim that foles would probably be  interested in the giants  i kind of think maybe foles and his  agents are trying  to bait the eagles  into tagging falls well now why would  you want to do that it's always better  to not be tagged well  maybe  just maybe  and i know sometimes when we speculate  people get their noses out of joint but  that's kind of what we do it's kind of  where there's value in understanding  how things have happened in the past  where the pieces are aligned now and  where they may go from here  what if  the agents who represent nick foles have  already  gauged the market for his services that  happens all the time it's tampering for  the teams to engage in the gauging of  the market but there are ways to do it  that are very discreet  that are very informative that are  hypothetical if need be but there's a  way to find out and usually the scouting  combine is the point where the facade is  dropped and people blatantly engage in  tampering about guys who are due to  become free agents but we've had weeks  now since the eagles ended their season  and people are trying to figure out what  nick foles is going to do it isn't all  that difficult to find a way to have  communications with the general managers  or head coaches or others with  organizations that may or may not be  interested in nick falls  and  if nick foles agents are learning  that  no one really wants to pay more than 25  million dollars a year on a long-term  deal  maybe his better play is to get tagged  and to sign it immediately whether  you're the backup in philly or whether  you get traded to jacksonville or  wherever else to lock in that 25 million  may be the way to go because if you do  hit the open market maybe you're not  going to get the kind of money  that you think you're going to get and  and stats you know for i got to give you  credit stats  it doesn't happen often but you had a  good point  you had a good point i'm going to  reluctantly give you praise  you raised a question that needed to be  raised  how many teams really do want nick falls  the the seat in denver is going to be  occupied by joe flacco we know that and  we know that the broncos considered  falls and opted for flacco which doesn't  say much for falls when you've got a  team picking flacco over falls now one  of the factors was polls is going to  cost more money but it's going to cost  more money i don't know because who else  is out there now you've got the jaguars  right that's a clear potential  destination because of the president of  john d filippo but other than the  jaguars where are the seats miami  i i i g i mean i guess brian flores the  new coach of the dolphins who saw up  close what foals did to the patriots  in the super bowl just  a year and less than a month ago could  be intrigued but you know what i have a  feeling that bill belichick was facing  nick foles twice a year he'd cracked  that code pretty quickly and he'd have  extra motivation to do it after what  happened in super bowl 52 so and and  here's the other thing too  for all these other teams that need  quarterbacks the dolphins who are we  talking about we're not talking about  nick falls we're talking about kyle  murray  you've got an incoming crop of young  cheap quarterbacks and what did we see  last year we saw five quarterbacks  drafted in round one and how many of  them are bust based upon one year none  what is that now i'm not saying that  these five guys are destined for  greatness and pro bowls and and busts in  canton but  the fact that as we approach draft 2019  the fact that draft 2018  was five for five with first round  quarterbacks is that going to result  in more quarterbacks or fewer  quarterbacks than otherwise would be  picked in round one this year it's gonna  cause a run on quarterbacks it's cheaper  it's a trend that is working we know  it's a copycat league so kyler murray  dwayne haskins drew lock  if you're a team that needs a  quarterback  are you going to lock in  with nick falls now  at 25 million or more per year  or are you going  to wait and see what happens in the  draft  i i just i think that  there's a real good chance  that nick falls people  have had the conversations they've  gauged the market and they've realized  probably better off with the 25 million  via the franchise tag from the  philadelphia eagles  i i i just have a feeling based upon and  that's the thing when you look at the  report from zack rosenblatt of nj.com  and i'm trying to provide him a  compliment here uh i'll see if i can do  it successfully  the actual nuts and bolts i look at and  i say who cares  right  but you think about it  you take a step back  you don't want to miss the forest for  the trees i never really did understand  that but it sounds good you don't want  to miss the forest for the trees the  forest here  is that maybe nick foles knows  that there isn't going to be a land rush  for nick foles if he hits the market as  an unrestricted free agent so the  question becomes  in this game of chess  checkers and ultimately chicken  are the eagles going to let him hit the  open market for  fear  of the possibility  that he stays in the division do they  use the franchise tag that's why  it's significant that someone  close to folds is saying he probably  would be interested in the giants we  don't even know if the giants are  interested in him  right maybe pat schumer is more  interested in case keenum maybe it's  going to be the same end result  that if the giants end up with case  keenum well first of all they could just  stick with eli manning but assuming  they're moving on from manning it could  be kingdom versus falls and while  kingdom's only 18 million dollars falls  is 25.  yeah  the events of this week  i think are significant as it relates to  what the interest will be in nick foles  and how much money will be a bail  available for nick foles and and  no matter what you do  and i think back to  when kurt warner had his resurgence in  arizona he wasn't handed that job  kurt warner had his time as the  quarterback for the greatest show-offs  on turf then he had that stretch  when it fell apart in st louis he was  with the giants and he got benched for  eli manning and there was just a sense  does he really have it anymore right uh  there's kind of that same so with foals  it's different because we've seen recent  postseason performances that we say oh  wow maybe he's got something but he had  that great 2013 when he had 27 touchdown  passes and two interceptions and at one  point chip kelly the coach of the eagles  declared he'd be the starter for the  next thousand years  and  then it fell off  and it's hard to set aside  that image of nick foles as the  quarterback of the rams and yes we can  blame jeff fisher we can blame the  offensive coordinator we can blame  everyone but nick foles  but if you're talking about  looking at the body of work and coming  to the conclusion that this guy's going  to make more than 25 million dollars a  year  one year after  the vikings handed 28 million per year  on a three-year contract fully  guaranteed to kirk cousins  and considering that last year all those  rookies taken in round one have worked  out  i i could see  quite possibly  a conclusion coming  that  nick foles isn't worth 25 million a year  and it could be  that  foles and his agents want the eagles to  pull the trigger on the franchise test  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

